(The number form of test 859: inside the branch the name is the number;
 after it, the top-level buffer, which the append grows.)
a buffer called hold is "abc".

To 'branchy' with a number called n.
    If n is 1 then,
        a number called hold is 5,
        Print "in branch {hold plus 1}".
    append "Z" to hold.
    Print "after {hold's size}".

'branchy' of 1.
'branchy' of 2.
